t  of a smile in the office let me tell you  that he said the government advice on  foreign travel has been  crystal clear even you've got a smirk at  that one well  all i was going to say is i announced it  actually friday a week ago at a press  conference in downing street uh and what  i said is actually if it's an amber or  red country please don't travel  uh for holidays it's for exceptional  circumstances and red is only for  essentially british citizens uh  returning so i can be completely  consistent and say the same thing today  that is the case we we are saying to  people  you know there's a heck of a lot of  hassle involved  in for example an amber country you've  got to take a pre-departure test you  then have to take two further tests  when you come home yet another one on  top of that if you wanted to  have tests to release after five days  you've got a quarantine  people will come to your house to check  your quality i mean it's expensive  it's not we're not at the stage of of  you know saying to people  um go to those places on a holiday in  fact please don't  green lists are for holidays and a  little bit of patience  as the world catches up with our vaccine  program  we'll get more of those countries opened  up as green countries  well and yet people are still going and  and travel agents and airlines and  everybody else are still  selling the holidays and the flights  well look we've moved away from a  situation where everything is  it's banned it's illegal i know we got  very used to this last year everything's  banned and illegal and you know  we're we're moving away from um that and  asking people to apply  a bit of common sense people asking for  guidance the answer is  actually for a red and amber list it's  not for going on  holiday but and you might say well i  have an amber i mean  i've heard this several times and let me  just explain that every country in the  world is put  into the amber category and then when  the joint biosecurity center  look at it they'll either say actually  this country has a particularly good  record they're doing all the uh all the  sequencing they're  they're on top of the problem they've  got high levels of vaccines it's a green  country  or there are real problems here it's a  red country  so the default is amber but amber is not  please go and visit there there's a lot  of cost and hassle  and quarantine required when you go to  those countries  and it is being very strictly enforced  um look  let's wrap back round to transport if if  we can i say  obviously you want more even more people  to go on the trains with this with this  new great british rail and  i know there's campaigns to get people  back on the buses and what have you  at the moment and what about mass  squaring when people are on  public transport should it happen would  you like to see it happen even if it's  not mandated well  right now you do have to wear a mask on  public transport unless you have an  exception  been very very pleased and impressed the  vast majority of people have been doing  it  it's been very good high levels of of  uptake  um that remains in place technically  it's in place until the 21st of june as  we know we'll have a  review that's the fourth stage of the  unlock and we'll be able to say more  about it  at that time but it is in fact the law  at the moment to wear  a mask and that's something that i think  people have just gotten used to doing  people  take their keys they take the wallet  that pick up the mask and they they  leave the home and we're seeing more  people  come back to transport as i say  cautiously but i hope in one direction  we are moving towards  a fuller unlock okay minister good to  talk to you this morning thank you

